WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Jai Shri Mataji, greetings to everyone.

2
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:10.780
We have a new feature I would like to tell you about: signing in.

3
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:17.390
If you are, for example, still working with the old page and

4
00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:23.290
you have no such button at the top left, let's take it in Ukrainian, "Sign in", then just

5
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:29.820
refresh the page, and it will appear. What does this

6
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:32.960
button give us? Let's find out.

7
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.040
In short,

8
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:42.030
it gives you a list of your own talks, gives

9
00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:48.970
an easier way to take on a review, automatic syncing and

10
00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:53.050
an easier hand-off for finalization.

11
00:00:54.260 --> 00:01:00.480
So if you open this portal and you

12
00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:05.140
do not have a GitHub account yet

13
00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:13.340
or are not signed in to GitHub in this browser, you will get this

14
00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:19.760
result: it asks you to sign in. So you can register right away if you have not

15
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:23.660
registered yet. Or if you already have one, you can sign in by one of the methods.

16
00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:27.780
I already have this passkey set up, so I sign in.

17
00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.920
And the result? Once I have signed in...

18
00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:38.520
Here my avatar shows up; it's sort of, well, not...

19
00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.580
It doesn't mean anything there.

20
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:46.880
You can set a photo in the GitHub settings, and it shows the name under which the

21
00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:52.200
sign-in was made. This is Slava Subotskyi. You also see a small halo here, and at the top

22
00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.840
a strip glows a little; on the dark theme you can see the glow better.

23
00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.220
This means we are signed in.

24
00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:06.580
What next? This gives us several things.

25
00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.960
First, the list of your own talks,

26
00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.460
right here.

27
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.580
We switch to "mine"; if you have none, it shows 0 here.

28
00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.500
If you have taken something on before, it shows up here.

29
00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.960
I have a list of six right now.

30
00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:32.360
If you are already registered on GitHub but have never worked with this portal,

31
00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:39.200
and have not passed on your login to be added to the project, then

32
00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:46.000
I'll show you now what it looks like. Here I have a work account. Let's click

33
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.000
"Sign in"

34
00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:54.200
and you see it's black and white; it says "Signed in as" ViacheslavSubotskyiJoinForma, with

35
00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.200
no write access.

36
00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:01.260
"Read-only features are available", "ask an administrator".

37
00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.840
So if you are in this state, black and white,

38
00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:13.740
and it says so, then you just need to... it means you have not started working

39
00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:18.360
with this project and have not passed on this e-mail to be added to it. Pass it on.

40
00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:25.720
Back to what else it gives us besides the list of your own talks.

41
00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:31.040
It is now a bit easier to take on a review.

42
00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.780
Let's try.

43
00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.420
We choose what we want to take for review.

44
00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:48.010
Guru Puja: "Take for review".

45
00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:53.770
We click, and it is already in "mine" automatically.

46
00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:57.620
There. Guru Puja is already here.

47
00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.240
With one button, and now it's done.

48
00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.900
That was the second.

49
00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.460
And the third: syncing.

50
00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:14.040
Remember? Before, our changes were stored only locally, and they had to be sent by a separate

51
00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.700
procedure.

52
00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:23.310
Now it is simpler. Let's go into any mode.

53
00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:30.100
Now you see there are no buttons here for sending anything.

54
00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.070
But now imagine we started editing.

55
00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:36.290
We edited the subtitles.

56
00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.480
Removed a full stop. We don't need that full stop.

57
00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:47.320
The moment we edit something, a cloud appears, and it

58
00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:50.560
now shows by its colour

59
00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:58.180
what is happening. If it is blue and says "Syncing…", it is in progress.

60
00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:03.280
Green means it is already "Synced"; red means something went wrong.

61
00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:10.930
That happens if there is no internet or something else, then it can be red.

62
00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.120
Otherwise it is only ever blue and green.

63
00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:18.780
So you don't need to touch it; it works automatically.

64
00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:19.700
Let's

65
00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:25.830
put a comma

66
00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:30.210
in; you see, it's blue again right away.

67
00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:35.250
It works in the background, just as when you work in a Google document, in the background

68
00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:39.550
it syncs automatically, and within a few seconds,

69
00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:46.720
up to a minute, while you work on the document, it syncs everything automatically.

70
00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:53.860
To make sure it is synced, you can click this cloud: "View

71
00:05:53.860 --> 00:06:00.620
on GitHub". You will see that something was already created in your name one minute

72
00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:01.620
ago.

73
00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:05.330
A submission like this was created,

74
00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:10.260
a few changes were made.

75
00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:19.180
And here is the result: in this subtitle the full stop was replaced with a comma.

76
00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:27.210
This is also an extra format, convenient for the system, which works and is then

77
00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:33.030
cleaned up. This syncing now works automatically; you don't need

78
00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:38.030
to know the processes for sending edits and so on.

79
00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:43.950
Imagine you made an edit by accident and don't actually need it.

80
00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:49.780
You undo it, clear it, and syncing happens as well, but

81
00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:54.870
the cloud is gone. Yes, if you have no edits,

82
00:06:56.330 --> 00:07:01.350
there is no cloud either, because there is nothing to sync; everything there is automatically

83
00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:06.030
cleaned up, if you decided to remove all your edits here.

84
00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:13.380
And how to finalize: the last thing I need to show.

85
00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.020
Say you have already finished editing.

86
00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:24.620
That's all you needed to do. Or let's do it here like this... Oh, something went

87
00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:25.620
wrong.

88
00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:35.780
It got cleared. I wanted to show it with another mode, the one with

89
00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:42.720
"Review translation". Let's remove some full stop here. Again

90
00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:46.400
the cloud appeared,

91
00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:53.020
now it will turn green, and let's say these are all the edits you wanted to make.

92
00:07:53.630 --> 00:08:00.450
Then you can actually mark your edit as one that is already

93
00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:07.350
ready. Let me show what it looks like. Here is ours, you see, a draft.

94
00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:14.220
That is, a draft, but if we click "Finalize — ready for review", that is, hand it

95
00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:18.860
over for a technical final review, a second review, you could say,

96
00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:22.500
then we click this button.

97
00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:29.800
"PR marked ready for review", it offers to open the PR, and you see, this same PR simply

98
00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:33.940
turned green. That is, it says it's done.

99
00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:40.810
You have done everything, you don't want to make more edits here; this is what

100
00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:46.930
now has to be passed on. And so a process starts here, the one that was

101
00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:47.930
talked about

102
00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:55.750
earlier: there are sync processes, and after them the technical part, which

103
00:08:55.750 --> 00:09:02.590
you don't need to care about. A technical person will look at it, to bring it

104
00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:05.510
to its final state.

105
00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:10.590
To sync all the needed files with each other: subtitles, transcript and so on.

106
00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:17.810
Your task as the reviewer now

107
00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:24.090
is just to make your edits. And when you have finished your edits,

108
00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:31.030
just click "Finalize — ready for review" at the end, and that's it.

109
00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:39.490
We revert the edits, and it should now clean our edits away.

110
00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.910
Cleaned up, closed.

111
00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:47.460
This is how the work goes now.

112
00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:52.500
I hope this makes the work easier, simpler and faster.

113
00:09:55.840 --> 00:10:02.300
If you have wishes about what to improve, what features to add,

114
00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:06.500
what is missing, what you feel could help your work,

115
00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:11.040
let us know. We will build it together.
